  "title": "osf review: multi-agent PR review pipeline",
  "summary": "Adds a full pull-request review subsystem to osf. A new `osf review run` selects review lenses for a change (from a shipped catalogue of 20, plus org and repo overrides), runs each configured coding-agent reviewer headless in a clean copy of the change, validates each answer against a JSON Schema, verifies every quoted finding against the real file, and reduces the answers to a per-lens and whole-review verdict. A new `review.yml` workflow builds osf from the base branch, runs each reviewer in its own job with only its own provider key, and a final job reduces and posts. Supporting pieces: an agent registry with review wiring, a work-item finder, secret redaction, a shared process-tree killer, and suppression ownership in the lint core.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
